' A let-assignment (no Set) to a member of a UDT that is of a class type. Here the class has a
' default member, so this is the VB6 idiom for setting its Value: VB6 runs it and leaves
' N = 5. In twinBASIC the project compiles with no diagnostic, and the build then fails with
' "compilation (codegen) error detected in 'Startup.Mainrootmain'". The same assignment to
' a local variable or to a field of a class works. So does Set h.o = ..., which is the
' way round it; without a default member (and without Set), h.o = p is the same codegen
' error, where a local variable gets error 91 at run time.
Module Startup

    Public Type Holder
        o As Widget
    End Type

    Public Sub Main()
        Dim h As Holder
        Set h.o = New Widget
        h.o = 5
        Debug.Print "N = " & h.o.N
    End Sub

End Module
